  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieves 48.5% acc, establishing RNA as the dominant modality, while config_010 (image_only, resnet50) is weak at 20.8%. We have very sparse evidence and haven't yet tested whether the profile/aggregation dimension matters for the stronger modality. Question: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is the most direct extension of config_001, changing only the profile setting from single to multi (with the necessary avgpool aggregation), while keeping the same encoder. This isolates the effect of multiprofile aggregation on RNA representation. Why best next: It builds on the strongest existing signal with a minimal, interpretable change. If multiprofile+avgpool improves over singleprofile, it validates the aggregation dimension and informs multimodal design (configs 018-027). If it does not improve, it tells us singleprofile suffices and we should focus budget on encoder quality or fusion strategy instead. This reduces the most critical uncertainty before committing experiments to more complex multimodal configurations."
}

